body:
V8 is frozen and will not be re-proposed unchanged.

The 24ce308 audit found one real D2 blocker: V8 made MissingTimestamp versus ArithmeticRefusal depend on operation provenance without requiring that provenance and its identity be derived from the checked packet or rescale operation. A caller could relabel identical INT64_MIN values or substitute a packet, extractor, or rescale receipt.

I chose the narrow V9 repair. The exact working-tree amendment now requires:
1. separate operation-specific checked packet normalization and exact rescaling;
2. no generic checked raw-value plus provenance/outcome-tag constructor;
3. packet, extractor, and rescale identities recomputed from complete canonical receipt preimages at decode/join boundaries;
4. provenance-flip, packet- and rescale-receipt substitution, supplied-ID mismatch, and exhaustive construction-door mutations on JVM/JS/Native;
5. positive controls proving lawful packet sentinel -> MissingTimestamp and actual unrepresentable rescale -> ArithmeticRefusal.

This adds no decoder, provider, dependency, media access, or runtime authority. Component-ledger and video-admission independent reviews of the exact amendment are underway. If they accept, I will supersede the D2 candidate and use collab as the live substitute second reviewer, with component consent. D2 remains documentation-only.
